{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>When I break.</b> A noun of action, and it comes as שבור, like בשכבה and בקומה. The meaning: I break the staff of bread, and it is by way of parable. And in Isaiah, 'the stay of bread,' for bread sustains the heart of man." "<b>Ten women.</b> For it is the full count, for the custom of Israel was to bake in every house its own oven, to eat all week, and the arrangement of the Sabbath proves it." "<b>And your bread shall be returned by weight.</b> Because it is little." "<b>And you shall eat and not be satisfied.</b> Sometimes there is famine yet the eater of little is satisfied, but you — though you eat much, you will not be satisfied."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:46.309804308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}